From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SheepyLord <37598021+SheepyLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 03:28:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The Remix menu and the HUD drawn into the back buffer under
 frame generation

With DLSS frame generation on, Alt+X took the game's input but drew no menu. The swapchain's present
blits the game's frame into the back buffer, then (patch 0094) the frame before its UI into the HUD-less
image beside it; the HUD and the Remix menu (ImGui_ImplDxvk::RenderDrawData) bind no target of their
own and draw into the one the last blit left bound: the HUD-less copy, which is only frame
generation's input and never shown. The HUD-less blit now comes first and the back buffer's last, so
the HUD and the menu are drawn into the presented image again, and the HUD-less copy stays without UI
(DLSS-G keeps the menu in place as UI). Frame generation off: nothing changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/d3d9/d3d9_swapchain.cpp | 13 ++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/d3d9/d3d9_swapchain.cpp b/src/d3d9/d3d9_swapchain.cpp
index d18d18f39..67855c5f3 100644
--- a/src/d3d9/d3d9_swapchain.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d9/d3d9_swapchain.cpp
@@ -1362,13 +1362,12 @@ namespace dxvk {
         { uint32_t(m_dstRect.right - m_dstRect.left), uint32_t(m_dstRect.bottom - m_dstRect.top) } };
       
 
-      m_blitter->presentImage(m_context.ptr(),
-        m_imageViews.at(imageIndex), dstRect,
-        swapImageView, srcRect);
-
       // NV-DXVK start: HUD-less frame generation input (GMod)
       // The frame before its UI goes beside the frame generation back buffer through the same blit, so a pixel no UI
-      // was drawn over comes out exactly as in the back buffer (rtx_dlfg_hudless.h).
+      // was drawn over comes out exactly as in the back buffer (rtx_dlfg_hudless.h). Before the back buffer's blit:
+      // the HUD and the Remix menu below draw into the render target the last blit leaves bound, which must be the
+      // back buffer. After it, they went into this copy, which is never shown: with frame generation on, Alt+X took
+      // the input and drew nothing.
       if (m_dlfgPresenter != nullptr && m_dlfgHudlessView != nullptr) {
         const Rc<DxvkImageView> hudless = m_dlfgPresenter->getHudlessView(imageIndex);
         if (hudless != nullptr) {
@@ -1377,6 +1376,10 @@ namespace dxvk {
       }
       // NV-DXVK end
 
+      m_blitter->presentImage(m_context.ptr(),
+        m_imageViews.at(imageIndex), dstRect,
+        swapImageView, srcRect);
+
       if (m_hud != nullptr)
         m_hud->render(m_context, info.format, info.imageExtent);
 
